`dsh-multi-key-rotation` is an independent work. It is not a fork of, and it
contains no source code from, `dsh-llm-key-rotation`. What it takes from that
project is the *idea* of rotating between several API keys of one LLM
provider when a quota is exhausted. The implementation, the pool model, the
quota probing, the reset-order selection, the settings page and every line of
code are original to this plugin.

What this plugin adds on top of that idea:

  * a pool the user configures by *pasting keys*, without naming environment
    variables by hand;
  * the pool *takes over the route* as soon as it loads, instead of waiting
    for the first failure;
  * remaining quota is probed per key and shown for both quota windows;
  * the next key is chosen by *reset order* — the key whose weekly window
    resets soonest is spent first;
  * the user can pin the key the provider starts with;
  * a MiniMax Token Plan quota signature (`2067`, `2056`) is recognized, so a
    spent plan rotates instead of failing the turn;
  * the configuration lives as a tab of the built-in Plugins settings section.
